  "title": "India's First Indigenous H5N1 Vaccine Against Bird Flu",
  "summary": "India unveils its first indigenous H5N1 vaccine to protect poultry from bird flu, with the vaccine developed by the National Institute of High Security Animal Diseases in Bhopal, marking a significant step in self-reliance and economic resilience.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Union Minister Shivraj Singh Chouhan unveiled the vaccine at the National Institute of High Security Animal Diseases in Bhopal.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The vaccine is the first-of-its-kind H5N1 virus against Clade 2.3.2.1a of HPAI.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It protects poultry and reduces economic losses for farmers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
