  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "India develops 1st indigenous H5N1 vaccine to protect poultry from bird flu",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/india-develops-1st-indigenous-h5n1-vaccine-to-protect-poultry-from-bird-flu-126112001123_1.html",
      "description": "Union Minister Shivraj Singh Chouhan unveils the country's first indigenous H5N1 vaccine, aimed at protecting poultry from bird flu and reducing economic losses for farmers.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-20T14:13:25"
    },
    {
      "title": "Shivraj Singh Chouhan unveils India's 1st home-grown H5N1 bird flu vaccine",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/agriculture/shivraj-singh-chouhan-unveils-india-s-1st-home-grown-h5n1-bird-flu-vaccine-126112000693_1.html",
      "description": "Union minister Shivraj Singh Chouhan unveiled the country's first indigenously developed H5N1 vaccine to protect chickens from bird flu here on Friday.\nThe vaccine has been developed by the ICAR-National Institute of High Security Animal Diseases in Bhopal, officials from the Union Agriculture Ministry said.\nThis is the first-of-its-kind vaccine developed in India against the H5N1 virus of Clade 2.3.2.1a of the highly pathogenic avian influenza (HPAI), they said.\nSpeaking on the occasion, Chouhan said, \"This vaccine is an example of India's self-reliance.\"\nHPAI, commonly known as bird flu, is a serious disease affecting chickens and other birds. Outbreaks can result in almost 100 per cent mortality among infected birds.\nBesides the Union Agriculture Minister, Madhya Pradesh Sports and Youth Welfare and Cooperatives Minister Vishwas Sarang and Bhopal BJP MP Alok Sharma, among others, were also present at the ceremony held here.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-20T10:22:47"
    }
  ]
